WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.672
The Princess and the Pea.

00:00:02.622 --> 00:00:09.741
Once upon a time there was a prince who wanted to marry a princess; but she would have to be a real princess.

00:00:09.741 --> 00:00:15.380
He travelled all over the world to find one, but nowhere could he get what he wanted.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:21.114
There were princesses enough, but it was difficult to find out whether they were real ones.

00:00:21.114 --> 00:00:25.298
There was always something about them that was not as it should be.

00:00:25.298 --> 00:00:31.657
So he came home again and was sad, for he would have liked very much to have a real princess.

00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:35.108
One evening a terrible storm came on.

00:00:35.108 --> 00:00:39.714
There was thunder and lightning, and the rain poured down in torrents.

00:00:39.714 --> 00:00:43.220
Suddenly a knocking was heard at the city gate.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.182
And the old king went to open it.

00:00:46.182 --> 00:00:50.108
It was a princess standing out there in front of the gate.

00:00:50.108 --> 00:00:52.649
But, good gracious!

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:56.304
What a sight the rain and the wind had made her look.

00:00:56.304 --> 00:01:03.777
The water ran down from her hair and clothes; it ran down into the toes of her shoes and out again at the heels.

00:01:03.777 --> 00:01:07.377
And yet she said that she was a real princess.

00:01:07.377 --> 00:01:11.440
Well, we'll soon find that out, thought the old queen.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:17.703
She went into the bed-room, took all the bedding off the bedstead, and laid a pea on the bottom.

00:01:17.703 --> 00:01:21.807
Then she took twenty mattresses and laid them on the pea.

00:01:21.807 --> 00:01:26.195
And then twenty eider-down beds on top of the mattresses.

00:01:26.195 --> 00:01:29.578
On this the princess had to lie all night.

00:01:29.578 --> 00:01:33.097
In the morning she was asked how she had slept.

00:01:33.097 --> 00:01:36.249
Oh, very badly!" said she.

00:01:36.249 --> 00:01:39.673
I have scarcely closed my eyes all night.

00:01:39.673 --> 00:01:47.581
Heaven only knows what was in the bed, but I was lying on something hard, so that I am black and blue all over my body.

00:01:47.581 --> 00:01:49.429
It's horrible!

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:58.029
Now they knew that she was a real princess, because she had felt the pea right through the twenty mattresses and the twenty eider-down beds.

00:01:58.029 --> 00:02:02.228
Nobody but a real princess could be as sensitive as that.

00:02:02.228 --> 00:02:07.989
So the prince took her for his wife, for now he knew that he had a real princess.

00:02:07.989 --> 00:02:13.926
And the pea was put in the museum, where it may still be seen, if no one has stolen it.

00:02:13.926 --> 00:02:16.820
There, that is a true story.

